WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.251
- Hello, have y'all ever met before?

00:00:03.251 --> 00:00:04.084
- We have not.

00:00:04.084 --> 00:00:04.917
- No.

00:00:04.917 --> 00:00:05.750
- Um, yeah no.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.419
- [Kelly] Oh, go ahead
with the accent, okay?

00:00:07.419 --> 00:00:08.661
It's so cute!

00:00:08.661 --> 00:00:09.494
- Yo, do you know what's really funny

00:00:09.494 --> 00:00:11.387
is I saw a cardboard
cutout of you backstage

00:00:11.387 --> 00:00:12.220
and I was like,

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.053
"Oh, my God."

00:00:13.053 --> 00:00:14.248
And like you were like
about to be singing as well,

00:00:14.248 --> 00:00:15.081
so I was like you know,

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:15.914
"Start with the show,"

00:00:15.914 --> 00:00:16.747
and everything,

00:00:16.747 --> 00:00:17.580
it was crazy,

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.413
but it wasn't you.

00:00:18.413 --> 00:00:19.246
- It's so funny 'cause that's happened

00:00:19.246 --> 00:00:20.079
to a lot of people here,

00:00:20.079 --> 00:00:20.912
because we have a cardboard cutout

00:00:20.912 --> 00:00:22.635
they like do rehearsals with

00:00:22.635 --> 00:00:24.009
and then I just do it like when I come,

00:00:24.009 --> 00:00:25.079
and people have literally run in,

00:00:25.079 --> 00:00:25.912
and been like, "Oh!"

00:00:25.912 --> 00:00:26.942
And then it's like, nope.

00:00:26.942 --> 00:00:28.979
Yeah, we just like to
fake people out here,

00:00:28.979 --> 00:00:30.338
we just like to mess with y'all.

00:00:30.338 --> 00:00:32.698
Well, we had a couple of
your Ted Lasso co-stars here,

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:34.745
they said that y'all got
to go to The White House,

00:00:34.745 --> 00:00:35.598
we saw a picture,

00:00:35.598 --> 00:00:36.470
was that so cool?

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.303
- It was crazy,

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:38.136
it was, yeah...

00:00:38.136 --> 00:00:38.969
It was nice,

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:40.062
I mean, like the president

00:00:40.062 --> 00:00:42.214
and the first lady were kind
enough to invite us over

00:00:42.214 --> 00:00:43.047
to you know,

00:00:43.047 --> 00:00:44.249
like talk about mental health with them

00:00:44.249 --> 00:00:45.324
and you know,

00:00:45.324 --> 00:00:46.157
like the aim was to you know,

00:00:46.157 --> 00:00:47.106
destigmatize it

00:00:47.106 --> 00:00:48.306
and it's an important-

00:00:48.306 --> 00:00:49.625
- Which is so great 'cause
Ted Lasso does that.

00:00:49.625 --> 00:00:50.935
- Yeah, it's an important
theme on our show

00:00:50.935 --> 00:00:52.101
and so, yeah we got to go down

00:00:52.101 --> 00:00:53.023
and speak to them,

00:00:53.023 --> 00:00:53.856
and it was yeah,

00:00:53.856 --> 00:00:54.689
it was crazy,

00:00:54.689 --> 00:00:55.658
I think halfway through
I was pinching myself,

00:00:55.658 --> 00:00:56.491
I was like,

00:00:56.491 --> 00:00:58.818
"How the hell have I ended
up at The White House?"

00:00:58.818 --> 00:00:59.651
- I'll tell you what,

00:00:59.651 --> 00:01:00.484
I've been to The White House

00:01:00.484 --> 00:01:01.317
and I heard,

00:01:01.317 --> 00:01:02.367
I didn't even know they
had a bowling alley,

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.607
but apparently, they have a bowling alley

00:01:04.607 --> 00:01:05.614
and you got to bowl there!

00:01:05.614 --> 00:01:06.447
- They do, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:06.447 --> 00:01:07.280
- [Kelly] What in the world?

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.113
- It was dope, yeah.

00:01:08.113 --> 00:01:09.540
- [Kelly] I'm not cool
enough to get that tour.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.943
- Aw man, I mean listen,

00:01:10.943 --> 00:01:11.913
we had to like slide-

00:01:11.913 --> 00:01:12.962
- Did you get a strike in The White House?

00:01:12.962 --> 00:01:14.410
- I didn't, Jason did,

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:15.962
Brendan did, Brett did,

00:01:15.962 --> 00:01:16.795
I did not.

00:01:16.795 --> 00:01:17.628
- Like, everyone did but you?

00:01:17.628 --> 00:01:19.378
Wow, that's horrible.

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:20.211
- Thanks Kelly.

00:01:20.211 --> 00:01:21.298
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:21.298 --> 00:01:22.570
- That's horrible.

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:23.810
Have you ever been to The White House?

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:24.643
- No!

00:01:24.643 --> 00:01:25.752
- Okay, so...

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:27.042
Okay, I've been there,

00:01:27.042 --> 00:01:28.232
but I never bowled,

00:01:28.232 --> 00:01:29.065
I was like,

00:01:29.065 --> 00:01:29.898
"That's so cool."

00:01:29.898 --> 00:01:30.731
- It's just such a shame,

00:01:30.731 --> 00:01:31.564
we didn't get to bowl
with the president though,

00:01:31.564 --> 00:01:32.397
that's the only thing,

00:01:32.397 --> 00:01:33.230
'cause I'd have smoked him,

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:34.063
I was like...

00:01:34.063 --> 00:01:34.896
That was my aim,

00:01:34.896 --> 00:01:35.729
I was like,

00:01:35.729 --> 00:01:36.562
as soon as they were like,

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:37.395
"Oh cool, like we get to
go to The White House."

00:01:37.395 --> 00:01:38.228
- I don't know if you would've smoked him,

00:01:38.228 --> 00:01:39.061
you were the one not doing strikes.

00:01:39.061 --> 00:01:40.347
(crowd laughing)

00:01:40.347 --> 00:01:42.431
So Toheeb, your momma's dream

00:01:42.431 --> 00:01:44.904
was for you to be the UK's first

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.049
Black prime minister, right?

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:48.552
Have you let her down you feel, or?

00:01:48.552 --> 00:01:49.811
- Disappointment 100%,

00:01:49.811 --> 00:01:51.100
like 'cause that was
the route that I was on,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.307
I was like a super academic kid in school

00:01:53.307 --> 00:01:54.926
and then like just for some reason

00:01:54.926 --> 00:01:56.846
just decided to U-turn into acting

00:01:56.846 --> 00:01:59.526
and for her it must've been
insanely surprising though,

00:01:59.526 --> 00:02:02.097
'cause it's like suddenly
your kid just might as well

00:02:02.097 --> 00:02:03.425
have told you he wants to be a clown

00:02:03.425 --> 00:02:05.486
and go to clown school

00:02:05.486 --> 00:02:06.319
and yeah.

00:02:06.319 --> 00:02:07.152
But you know,

00:02:07.152 --> 00:02:07.985
I went to drama school

00:02:07.985 --> 00:02:09.137
and once you know,

00:02:09.137 --> 00:02:11.527
we started on our way with acting,

00:02:11.527 --> 00:02:12.927
yeah she was insanely supportive.

00:02:12.927 --> 00:02:14.286
So, my thing was always,

00:02:14.286 --> 00:02:16.097
"I'm not gonna be the UK's
first Black prime minister,

00:02:16.097 --> 00:02:18.057
but I might play him in a show one day."

00:02:18.057 --> 00:02:18.890
- I know, that's...

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:20.297
I'm so curious,

00:02:20.297 --> 00:02:23.426
like that's such a cool
thing to be active in

00:02:23.426 --> 00:02:24.259
like as a kid,

00:02:24.259 --> 00:02:26.919
like what do you think
made you pivot into acting?

00:02:26.919 --> 00:02:28.439
- I mean, I had some really dope teachers,

00:02:28.439 --> 00:02:29.938
but I don't know,

00:02:29.938 --> 00:02:31.658
I think there's something about you know,

00:02:31.658 --> 00:02:34.237
like being a kid with a funny accent,

00:02:34.237 --> 00:02:35.306
I came from Nigeria

00:02:35.306 --> 00:02:36.986
and there's something about performing

00:02:36.986 --> 00:02:39.029
that is a way to you know,

00:02:39.029 --> 00:02:40.627
you can hide in your characters I guess

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.058
and so, like that became a thing

00:02:42.058 --> 00:02:42.909
where it was like,

00:02:42.909 --> 00:02:43.877
I didn't feel so isolated

00:02:43.877 --> 00:02:45.007
when I was a part of a company

00:02:45.007 --> 00:02:46.007
or you know,

00:02:46.007 --> 00:02:47.858
doing plays or hiding in a character

00:02:47.858 --> 00:02:49.157
and so yeah,

00:02:49.157 --> 00:02:51.266
that kinda just became
my escape in a little way

00:02:51.266 --> 00:02:53.267
and then it became the
thing where I was like,

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:56.756
"If I'm doing law every day
for the rest of my life,

00:02:56.756 --> 00:02:57.778
I'm gonna be pretty miserable,

00:02:57.778 --> 00:02:58.927
but if I'm doing this thing,

00:02:58.927 --> 00:03:00.257
then I might not be that sad."

00:03:00.257 --> 00:03:01.090
So, yeah-

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:02.912
- Well, I can tell your
mom is super proud,

00:03:02.912 --> 00:03:03.745
I'm a momma,

00:03:03.745 --> 00:03:07.042
yeah, you're proud any time
your kid like finds themselves,

00:03:07.042 --> 00:03:07.875
I said selves,

00:03:07.875 --> 00:03:08.708
how many are in there?

00:03:08.708 --> 00:03:09.541
Finds themself

00:03:09.541 --> 00:03:10.776
and like really loves what they're doing,

00:03:10.776 --> 00:03:12.169
and is passionate about it, that's cool.

00:03:12.169 --> 00:03:13.401
- You're also making money.

00:03:13.401 --> 00:03:14.331
- Yeah, there's that,

00:03:14.331 --> 00:03:15.164
there's that.

00:03:15.164 --> 00:03:16.312
You know, it's like I've moved out,

00:03:16.312 --> 00:03:17.145
like, do you know what I mean?

00:03:17.145 --> 00:03:17.978
I can afford to live by myself.

00:03:17.978 --> 00:03:19.149
- [Kelly] Like, "Oh, we
can afford to do this."

00:03:19.149 --> 00:03:19.982
- My brother

00:03:19.982 --> 00:03:20.815
and I might be eating like bread,

00:03:20.815 --> 00:03:21.939
and water every day, but-

00:03:21.939 --> 00:03:22.772
- Oh my God,

00:03:22.772 --> 00:03:23.605
I lived on ramen.

00:03:23.605 --> 00:03:24.838
I lived on ramen,

00:03:24.838 --> 00:03:25.671
that's all I ate.

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:26.753
- Yo, have you ever tried Indomie?

00:03:26.753 --> 00:03:29.293
It's like Nigerian ramen noodles,

00:03:29.293 --> 00:03:31.460
I'm gonna find a way to like grab you some

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.293
and get you some...

00:03:32.293 --> 00:03:33.126
I mean, your probably don't eat-

00:03:33.126 --> 00:03:33.959
- I love ramen,

00:03:33.959 --> 00:03:35.529
yeah, I try everything.

00:03:35.529 --> 00:03:36.808
I was very lucky,

00:03:36.808 --> 00:03:39.539
so from 19 I ended up traveling
like all over the world,

00:03:39.539 --> 00:03:41.038
so I've been to a lot of different places,

00:03:41.038 --> 00:03:42.288
so I'll try anything,

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.441
I won't love everything,

00:03:43.441 --> 00:03:44.274
but I'll try it.

00:03:44.274 --> 00:03:45.107
- Let me know how you go,

00:03:45.107 --> 00:03:45.940
I'm actually gonna, yeah.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:46.773
That's my mission,

00:03:46.773 --> 00:03:47.606
I'm gonna get you some Indomie.

00:03:47.606 --> 00:03:48.502
- Okay, I like this mission.

00:03:48.502 --> 00:03:49.435
I'm willing to do this.

00:03:49.435 --> 00:03:51.286
- Do I get some?

00:03:51.286 --> 00:03:52.406
- [Toheeb] That was a given.

00:03:52.406 --> 00:03:53.564
- [Kelly] He's gonna bring
it to improv over there.

00:03:53.564 --> 00:03:56.346
- [Toheeb] Everyone I meet gets Indomie.

00:03:56.346 --> 00:03:57.354
- Perfect.

00:03:57.354 --> 00:03:59.994
- So, I wanna ask about
your new show, The Power.

00:03:59.994 --> 00:04:00.994
What can you tell us about it?

00:04:00.994 --> 00:04:01.827
It looks kinda...

00:04:01.827 --> 00:04:03.135
Like, why are you not allowed to be there?

00:04:03.135 --> 00:04:04.147
They (indistinct) not like you there.

00:04:04.147 --> 00:04:05.170
- Because I'm a man.

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.871
No, it's set in a world where women,

00:04:07.871 --> 00:04:10.042
young women especially
generate this ability,

00:04:10.042 --> 00:04:12.931
almost overnight to generate electricity

00:04:12.931 --> 00:04:13.764
through their hands

00:04:13.764 --> 00:04:16.655
and electrocute people at will-

00:04:16.655 --> 00:04:17.488
- Cool power.

00:04:17.488 --> 00:04:18.512
- [Toheeb] Yeah, insane.

00:04:18.512 --> 00:04:19.345
- Yeah.

00:04:19.345 --> 00:04:20.354
- And so, like overnight they become

00:04:20.354 --> 00:04:22.125
the physically superior gender

00:04:22.125 --> 00:04:24.174
and my character's a journalist,

00:04:24.174 --> 00:04:26.535
and unknowingly breaks this story,

00:04:26.535 --> 00:04:27.368
and you know,

00:04:27.368 --> 00:04:29.003
like puts this video out on the internet

00:04:29.003 --> 00:04:31.630
and suddenly, like amasses this you know,

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:32.590
following, and platform,

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:35.083
and becomes a bit of a spokesperson,

00:04:35.083 --> 00:04:36.631
and a mouthpiece for this new thing.

00:04:36.631 --> 00:04:38.388
And he goes on this
really interesting journey

00:04:38.388 --> 00:04:39.221
of you know,

00:04:39.221 --> 00:04:40.054
finding himself,

00:04:40.054 --> 00:04:40.887
finding purpose

00:04:40.887 --> 00:04:42.196
and figuring out what he wants to do

00:04:42.196 --> 00:04:43.706
with his platform, you know?

00:04:43.706 --> 00:04:45.645
Like, finding his own
power in the media almost

00:04:45.645 --> 00:04:48.475
and yeah, it's a pretty amazing story,

00:04:48.475 --> 00:04:50.328
like we have a lot of
brilliant characters,

00:04:50.328 --> 00:04:51.718
an incredible cast

00:04:51.718 --> 00:04:53.470
and yeah, I can't wait
to share it with people.

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:54.731
- I like the parallel too,

00:04:54.731 --> 00:04:56.630
with like even women's
rights being taken away,

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:58.901
like of how they have
you know electricity,

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:00.362
then they're trying to take it, right?

00:05:00.362 --> 00:05:01.195
I'm assuming-

00:05:01.195 --> 00:05:02.063
- Oh 100%, yeah.

00:05:02.063 --> 00:05:03.133
People aren't just gonna be like,

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:04.311
"Oh yeah, great.

00:05:04.311 --> 00:05:05.144
Run the world."

00:05:05.144 --> 00:05:06.863
- Yeah, yeah exactly, exactly.

00:05:06.863 --> 00:05:09.925
- It would be really cool
though to be like, "Beep!"

00:05:09.925 --> 00:05:11.874
Just for sometimes.

00:05:11.874 --> 00:05:12.707
We need another...

00:05:12.707 --> 00:05:14.413
This is why God didn't allow it.

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:15.405
We need another break,

00:05:15.405 --> 00:05:17.811
Ted Lasso season three is on Apple TV+

00:05:17.811 --> 00:05:20.082
and also check out The Power, everybody.

00:05:20.082 --> 00:05:21.621
New episodes premiere every Friday,

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:22.777
exclusively on Prime Video.

